# Ebb — Seats

## Contract

The seat contract — what a seat is, seat accounting, the rules, launching, and the standing prompt — is `contracts/SEATS.md`, copied verbatim into `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md` at install. It is not reproduced here, and it is not edited per-project.

This specimen shows only what the interview writes: the roster below.

## This project

### Roster

| Seat | Role brief | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `seat-worker-1` | `fleet/WORKER.md` | Primary implementation |
| `seat-reviewer` | `crew/REVIEWER.md` | Never authors what it reviews |
| (commander) | this folder's `CLAUDE.md` | The principal's own session |

Minimum viable fleet for this project. A second worker goes in when the reviewer is idle waiting for work; a designer goes in when the principal is spending more time decomposing beads than deciding direction.
